From ef068088aea3692fc1ac4f9ec525a33eec1ec064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Native: a desktop build of the game (spike)

The game's C compiled for a PC (32-bit, -m32), with the GBA's memory regions
mapped at their own addresses, C versions of the hand-written ARM routines,
the overlays linked into the image, and a software stand-in for the display
drawn line by line with the HBlank DMA and interrupts. A headless front end
runs the arena's smoke scripts and writes PNG shots; an SDL3 front end opens
a window. It boots into the arena and fights a battle to the win.

Everything is in port/ (port/README.md). Upstream files get hooks under
NATIVE: system/asm.h (the inline assembly), system/task.h
(TASK_IN_OVERLAY), Overlay_Load; and a UBFIX guard for the Battle Arena's
first placement, which shares a sprite with no previous actor. The GBA
build is unchanged (same ROM).

Gaps: no sound, battle effects draw nothing (the blitter's fragments are
stubs), null stores the cartridge ignores crash (the field Psynergy menu).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8ymW43oDEDKD8HswP83
